# TF-C85 — the CHECKED-IN expected reached pragma vocabulary, per predefine class.
# Each class is censused on the leg whose corpus it is (pe on Windows, elf on Linux, macho on the Mac):
#   dssharness run pragma-profile-census --legs <leg> --input manifest=<that leg's corpus manifest>   (the check)
#   dssharness run pragma-profile-census-update --legs <leg> --input manifest=<...>   (regenerates this file into the
#   step's kept output, never in place; review it, pull it back from a remote leg, and replace this file with it)
# Format: <class> <pragma-leading-word> <count>.   `#` lines are documentation.
#
# ★★ THIS IS A FLOOR, NOT A TOTAL, AND THE DIFF IS EXPECTED TO MOVE. A reached-set
# depends on the manifest's defines, on the predefine class, and on HOW FAR EACH TU
# GETS before a hard error stops it. All three change as other cycles land.
#
# HISTORY (the measurements the lines below replaced are in git; each is kept here as what it taught):
#   * 2026-07-29, ONE manifest (the WSL corpus) under all three classes: pe 2135 (warning 1685, intrinsic 448,
#     optimize 2 -- all MSVC vocabulary under `#if defined(_MSC_VER)`, which the pe profile then defined), macho 20,
#     elf nothing. TF-C86 raised macho to 38 (pack 8 -> 22, mark new) as un-blocked TUs got further: the
#     floor-not-total rule, observed.
#   * 2026-10-01 (P69 lane hm): that design measured NOTHING on either host -- a manifest is one platform's corpus
#     (another class stops at its first line, `windows.h` not found), and the pe profile no longer defines
#     `_MSC_VER` (mingw-w64's GNU-on-Windows identity), so the MSVC vocabulary is reached by no leg. Each class is
#     censused over its own corpus since, and a sentinel pragma in every TU proves the disarmed config ran.
#   * 2026-10-06 (P69 lane hm), that design's first measurement, each class on its own leg with that leg's build:
#     in pe (windows-x86_64-debug), elf (linux-x86_64-debug) and macho (macos-arm64-release) the sentinel spoke in
#     all 189 TUs of the leg's own corpus and no pragma besides it -- so no data line follows. macho's 2026-07-29
#     lines (clang 12, mark 4, pack 22) were the WSL corpus compiled under the macho class, a corpus no leg
#     compiles as macho.
#   * 2026-10-06 (P69 lane hm, the re-review's MAJOR 1): one leading sentinel proved only that a TU STARTED. Each TU
#     has an opening and a closing sentinel since, and a run is refused unless both speak in every TU, no error but
#     an unclaimed pragma appears and no pragma diagnostic is elided. Under that, pe and elf matched again: both
#     sentinels in 189 of 189 TUs, no other error (macho not re-run: the Mac was unreachable that night).
#   * 2026-10-07 (P69 lane hm): macho on that design too, on its own leg with that leg's build (macos-arm64-release,
#     AppleClang 21.0.0, run 20261007-164226-1d84c3e9): both sentinels in 189 of 189 TUs, no other error -- it
#     matched, so all three classes match under the two-sentinel design.
